layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p
    | The
    strong backlog
    | holds the factory's
    strong packages
    | : large pieces of work, each one taken from start to finish by one worker. The
    a(href="/docs/coordinator") coordinator
    | picks them from here, records how they did at each gate, and asks you when it cannot decide alone. You watch,
    | answer and, when needed, stop or revert from your phone.

  h2#board The board
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="backlog-desktop.png" alt="The backlog on a desktop: the governor banner with the 5-hour and 7-day usage bars, then six columns of package cards from Backlog to Blocată." caption="The backlog on a desktop, one column per status.")
  p
    | Open
    strong Backlog
    | in the menu. On a desktop each status is a column; on a phone you pick a status at the top and see one list. A
    | card shows the package's id and title, the G1 to G5 gate chips, its cost, and these marks:
  ul
    li
      strong ready
      | : it is Gata and everything it depends on is integrated, so it can start now.
    li
      strong waits on …
      | : the packages it still waits for.
    li
      strong sensitive
      | : authentication, access rules, imports or pseudonymisation; such packages get an extra security review and are
      | marked in the digest.
    li An open stop or revert request.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="backlog-phone.png" alt="The backlog on a phone: the governor banner, a row of status filters with counts, and a list of package cards." caption="On a phone, filter by status." phone)

  h3#statuses The six statuses
  dl
    dt Backlog
    dd Written down, not ready yet.
    dt Gata
    dd Specified and ready to start once its dependencies are integrated.
    dt În lucru
    dd A worker has it.
    dt La porți
    dd The work is done and the gates are running.
    dt Integrată
    dd It passed the gates and was merged.
    dt Blocată
    dd It failed the gates three times, or something outside it stops it.

  h3#governor-banner The banner at the top
  p
    | It shows the
    a(href="/docs/coordinator#governor") governor's
    | answer: whether new workers may start, or until when the factory waits, with the 5-hour and 7-day usage and how
    | old that data is.

  h2#new Adding packages
  p
    | Use
    strong New task
    | on the board, also from a phone: a title, an optional id (such as
    code P3
    | ; otherwise one like
    code T12
    | is made), a description, the acceptance criteria one per line, what it depends on, its status and its priority.
    | Higher priority starts first among ready packages.

  h3#markdown Importing from Markdown
  p
    | A package can live as a Markdown file in any repository: frontmatter between two
    code ---
    | lines, then the description. Upload the files on the board, or run
    a(href="/docs/commands#tasks-import") bb tasks import
    | with a file or a folder. Importing the same id again updates the package and keeps its status, unless the file
    | sets one.
  pre
    code
      | ---
      | id: P2
      | title: Inventory
      | status: gata
      | depends_on: [P1]
      | priority: 10
      | sensitive: false
      | ---
      | What the package covers.
      |
      | ## Acceptance criteria
      | - Stock moves post to the ledger
      | - The monthly report matches the old one
  p
    code after
    | works as well as
    code depends_on
    | , and the criteria can also be an
    code acceptance
    | list in the frontmatter.

  h3#github Importing GitHub issues
  p
    | With a GitHub token in
    a(href="/docs/settings") Settings
    | , the board can import a repository's open issues, optionally only those with a given label. Pull requests are
    | skipped, and importing again updates the same packages.

  h2#package A package's page
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="task-desktop.png" alt="A package page on a desktop: header with status, branch and cost, the acceptance criteria, and the gates G1 to G5 with verdicts, summaries and a screenshot thumbnail." caption="A package with its gates and their screenshots.")
  p
    | Tap a card to open its page: status (you can change it), repository, branch, cost, the prompt and its version,
    | the Claude Code session and herdr terminal working on it, the acceptance criteria, its dependencies and its full
    | history.

  h3#gates The gates
  p Each gate shows its latest verdict, its summary and any screenshots; earlier attempts fold away below it.
  dl
    dt G1
    dd Typecheck, lint, unit and end-to-end tests.
    dt G2
    dd Acceptance tests written before the work by another agent, which the worker cannot change.
    dt G3
    dd An independent review with a structured verdict.
    dt G4
    dd Screenshots at desktop and phone width, judged against the design rules.
    dt G5
    dd Rebase on main, then G1 and G2 again on the result.

  h3#stop Stopping or reverting
  p
    strong Oprește pachetul
    | asks the coordinator to stop work on this package.
    strong Cere revenirea integrării
    | asks it to revert the package's merge. Both only record your request, with an optional note: the coordinator
    | reads it and does the git work, because Buildyboy never runs git on your repositories. The page shows whether it
    | has picked the request up yet.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="task-phone.png" alt="A package page on a phone: the gates as a list, followed by the Oprește pachetul and Cere revenirea integrării buttons." caption="The same package on a phone." phone)

  h3#launch Starting a package
  p
    | A package can also be started from its page on one of your machines: as an interactive agent in a new herdr
    | terminal (the default, so it stays visible and correctable), or as a one-shot
    a(href="/docs/jobs") job
    | . Both need the machine's
    a(href="/docs/runner") runner
    | , and the folder must be inside its allowed roots.

  h2#decisions Decisions
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="decisions-desktop.png" alt="The Decisions page: a pending question with its context and one button per option, and answered questions below." caption="A question from the coordinator, waiting for you.")
  p
    | When the coordinator cannot settle something alone, it asks you. The question arrives as a notification and waits
    | on the
    strong Decisions
    | page (the Inbox links to it, and the attention bar counts it). Tap one of the offered answers or write your own;
    | the coordinator reads it the next time it checks. Cancel a question that no longer matters.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="decisions-phone.png" alt="The Decisions page on a phone, with option buttons sized for a thumb." caption="Answering from a phone." phone)

  h2#digest The daily digest
  p
    | Once a day, at the time set in Settings → Factory (08:00 by default, the server's time), a notification sums up
    | the last 24 hours: what was integrated, which gates passed or failed, what is in progress or blocked, usage and
    | the governor, and the decisions and requests still waiting. The coordinator can send one at any time, and so can
    | you from Settings.
